Spoiler! And bug??

There was a thread a while back about making multiple Excaliburs by
dipping groups of long swords.  I contended that it wouldn't work
because you can't pick up long swords in groups, only missile weapons 
allow this.

It turns out I was wrong.  I tested it in wizard mode.  I had 11 arrows,
and kept zapping them with a wand of polymorph.  Evenually I got 11
long swords.  I picked them all up -- as a group in one slot -- and
dipped them all into various fountains.  Sure enough, A blessed hand
reached up and gave me 11 Excaliburs.

This may not be a wise practice though.  What if a group of hill orcs
each got an Excalibur?

Another question: Do you do 11x damage with eleven swords?
